# origin/main behaviour (baseline per maintainer decision 6)
# Generated by TestLegacyMenuSystemDetails (pkg/characterization); regenerate with -update. Do not edit.
# Screen: System Details (main menu 9), SSH_CLIENT set, q (pkg/menu), run in a child process
# Script: stdin "q\n", not a terminal, so nothing typed is echoed
# Tools on PATH (stand-ins): lastlog, lscpu, nproc
# dryRun false; TZ=UTC
# Masked, read from the machine the test runs on, no seam: the OS, Hostname, User and Load lines, the addresses (one line for however many), and Domain, dropped. Their padding goes with them.
# Pauses: 0 ("Press Enter to ..."; origin/main says "Press any key to ...", DEV-050)
# KNOWN-DEFECT: "CPU Freq: 0.00 GHz": collectCPUInfo sets the frequency only where the host-info service gave no CPU model or nproc failed (collectors.go:199-205, :231, :246-252), so with both, the usual case, it is 0.00 on every host [I, not run on a host].
# KNOWN-DEFECT: "Memory: 3.89/7.78 GiB" counts MemFree as all that is free (used = total - free, collectors.go:329), with MemAvailable 5.83 GiB in this /proc/meminfo (host_info/debian.golden holds MemoryFree): page cache reads as used.
# KNOWN-DEFECT: Disk sizes are bytes / 1024^3 labelled "GB" (collectors.go:430-432, display.go:104), where memory, the same division, says "GiB" (:370, :112).
# NOTE: The screen clears itself on every draw (system_details_menu.go:38; utils.go:24-25), the report and all above it gone from the terminal's screen.
# NOTE: Everything the screen reads is read again on each draw, four GetHostInfo's among them: collectOSInfo, collectCPUInfo, collectMemoryInfo, collectDiskInfo each call it (collectors.go:35, :198, :324, :380), counted below.
# NOTE: No section headings: blank lines alone part the report (display.go:46-49 and so on), two of them each time. The title prints twice, the box's top line and its shade (display.go:36; boxes.go:194-292).
# The screen as printed, ESC as the four characters \x1b, each line ending in $; <no-newline> marks text with no final newline.
# ----
